<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?><?xml-stylesheet href="http://www.blogger.com/styles/atom.css" type="text/css"?><feed xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom' xmlns:openSearch='http://a9.com/-/spec/opensearchrss/1.0/' xmlns:gd="http://schemas.google.com/g/2005"><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post155243576422233818..comments</id><updated>2017-04-13T04:47:21.148-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Comments on Pro Libertate: The Default Setting is &quot;Overkill&quot; (UPDATED; see the bottom of the essay)</title><link rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#feed' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/feeds/comments/default'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html'/><link rel="hub" href="http://pubsubhubbub.appspot.com/"/><author><name>William N. Grigg</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/14368220509514750246</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='32' height='19' src='http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-5rhFUXs_62I/VgVL2E3rMII/AAAAAAAAMJ4/cjJOyI7W208/s220/Photo%2BRon%2BPaul%2BLiberty%2BReport.jpg'/></author><generator version='7.00' uri='http://www.blogger.com'>Blogger</generator><openSearch:totalResults>8</openSearch:totalResults><openSearch:startIndex>1</openSearch:startIndex><openSearch:itemsPerPage>25</openSearch:itemsPerPage><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7486455062310215083</id><published>2007-05-06T14:14:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-06T14:14:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>drfix -- I seem to have been paid a visit by Senor...</title><content type='html'>drfix -- I seem to have been paid a visit by Senor Moment: I&#39;d assumed that the e-mail address was on my profile. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Here it is: WNGrigg@msn.com</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/7486455062310215083'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/7486455062310215083'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html?showComment=1178482440000#c7486455062310215083' title=''/><author><name>William N. Grigg</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/14368220509514750246</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='25' height='32' src='http://www.weekendinterviewshow.com/pics/grigg.jpg'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-155243576422233818' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/155243576422233818' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1344012943"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 6, 2007 at 2:14 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3625902218211651035</id><published>2007-05-06T11:36:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-06T11:36:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Will, thanks for the encouragement.  It&#39;s not fun ...</title><content type='html'>Will, thanks for the encouragement.  It&#39;s not fun but on the flip side I can honestly say I have never been as relaxed, or feel as free, as I am right now.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;To not have a gun to my head to &quot;perform&quot; to someone else&#39;s expectations is something I have never experienced in all my life.  So its allowed me to contemplate that maybe God has something special in store for the family and myself.  &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;The kinds of opportunities that this jobless &quot;sabbatical&quot; allow don&#39;t come around often in life, so I&#39;m really looking for answers.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;And, on another note, just how would I drop you an email message?  I can&#39;t find any means of sending my thoughts but through this blog!.... hahahah!&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;On the Star Trek, teenage boy love interest, angle.  Yeoman Rand was hot!...  Looking back, as an older and hopefully wiser man, I realize how my hormonal chains were being vigorously yanked!</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/3625902218211651035'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/3625902218211651035'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html?showComment=1178472960000#c3625902218211651035' title=''/><author><name>DrFix</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/13996714804361467430</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-155243576422233818' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/155243576422233818' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-388975791"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 6, 2007 at 11:36 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8631758731404086699</id><published>2007-05-06T00:04:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-06T00:04:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Will -Actually, I always looked at Troi as a bit o...</title><content type='html'>Will -&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Actually, I always looked at Troi as a bit of a buttinski, but she was easy on the eyes. We could go back and forth for quite some time about the babes of Star Trek, but I won&#39;t. There were several that were very attractive, and a few of them still look good even at their current age.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;The first time I met Grace Lee Whitney I told her I&#39;d had a crush on her since I was 13. On Sept. 8, 1966, I watched the very first episode of TOS (I was 13 years old) and have been a pretty obsessed fan ever since. I&#39;m pretty sure I fell in love with Yeoman Rand that year. Anyway, there sure were some great women on that show, and I appreciate your devotion to your wife.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/8631758731404086699'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/8631758731404086699'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html?showComment=1178431440000#c8631758731404086699' title=''/><author><name>Mister Spock</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/04790678390017800846</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-155243576422233818' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/155243576422233818' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1307178746"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 6, 2007 at 12:04 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4780376893405146384</id><published>2007-05-05T23:31:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-05T23:31:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Mister Spock -- Given the tone of your comments ab...</title><content type='html'>Mister Spock -- &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Given the tone of your comments about Marina Sirtis, am I correct in assuming that you are deep in the Plak Tow? &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Whether we&#39;re discussing Ms. Sirtis or her dramatic doppleganger, Counselor Troi, the individual in question is quite lovely. But she is easily eclipsed by the sight or even the thought of Korrin; it is as if we sought to find Aldebaran while that faint and distant star shared the noonday sky with our own Sun. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;(Besides, as a single man I was much more partial to Beverly Crusher/Gates McFadden, anyway.)</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/4780376893405146384'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/4780376893405146384'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html?showComment=1178429460000#c4780376893405146384' title=''/><author><name>William N. Grigg</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/14368220509514750246</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='25' height='32' src='http://www.weekendinterviewshow.com/pics/grigg.jpg'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-155243576422233818' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/155243576422233818' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1344012943"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 5, 2007 at 11:31 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4112893893308785077</id><published>2007-05-05T20:46:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-05T20:46:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Will-I saw the video of the woman trying to get to...</title><content type='html'>Will-&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;I saw the video of the woman trying to get to the hospital the other night on Bill O&#39;Reilly&#39;s show. (It was an accident, I didn&#39;t mean to be watching him.) I was going to see if I could find a link to it and send it to you, but someone beat me to it. Another fine example of a LEO (not a peace officer) abusing citizens.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;But my main reason for writing was your comment re Counselor Troi. Are you having vision problems? I had my picture taken with Marina Sirtis at the opening of Star Trek: The Experience in Las Vegas about 9 years ago (I took the tour/ride with a group of Paramount and Hilton executives), and she is even better looking in person - especially when her hair is straight. Perhaps a good opthamologist?</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/4112893893308785077'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/4112893893308785077'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html?showComment=1178419560000#c4112893893308785077' title=''/><author><name>Mister Spock</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/04790678390017800846</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-155243576422233818' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/155243576422233818' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1307178746"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 5, 2007 at 8:46 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-5044328555245808123</id><published>2007-05-05T11:55:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-05T11:55:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Dr., I&#39;m so sorry to hear that you&#39;ve been left jo...</title><content type='html'>Dr., I&#39;m so sorry to hear that you&#39;ve been left jobless. It&#39;s not a whole lot of fun, is it?&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Please drop me an e-mail to tell me how you&#39;re doing, and to let me know if there&#39;s anything I can do to help. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;The really weird thing is that although I&#39;m nominally unemployed (the work I do for pay is on a contract/freelance basis), I&#39;ve been working as much as I did before the JBS fired me. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;It&#39;s been a blessing, in an ironic way, to be working out of home even in our present circumstances. Korrin is doing much better, but she&#39;s still bedridden quite a bit. So I can help the boys get off to school and take care of the girls while Korrin gets the rest she still needs.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Here&#39;s something weird, followed by a praise note. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Because of Korrin&#39;s repeated hospitalization, we get regular visits from a person called a &quot;counselor.&quot; When I first heard this was going to happen, I sarcastically quipped: &quot;So Deanna Troi makes house calls?&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Well, oddly enough, our counselor Penny looks A LOT like Deanna Troi. (For the record, I don&#39;t find Troi particularly attractive.) &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;A couple of months ago, Penny showed up and suggested that we sign up for State grants to pay our rent, buy groceries, and pay for auto repairs. &quot;Your family will certainly qualify,&quot; she said. &quot;Why don&#39;t I just get you started?&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;I gestured for Penny to come close enough to hear me whisper my reply:&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&quot;I really appreciate that, but unless we&#39;re facing absolute destitution, I really can&#39;t do that.&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;She nodded her understanding, and repeated that the grants &quot;are there if you need them.&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&quot;Great,&quot; I thought to myself. &quot;Is this principle, or merely self-aggrandizing pride?&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Now -- here comes the REALLY COOL part of this story.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;NOT A DAY LATER I was contacted by a couple of very good friends from Texas who, in a gesture of sacrificial love, sent our family enough money to get us through that month and most of the next, a period during which I wasn&#39;t able to make any money as a contractor and freelancer. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;As a believer, I know better than to consider that to be a coincidence. God is good.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/5044328555245808123'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/5044328555245808123'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html?showComment=1178387700000#c5044328555245808123' title=''/><author><name>William N. Grigg</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/14368220509514750246</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='25' height='32' src='http://www.weekendinterviewshow.com/pics/grigg.jpg'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-155243576422233818' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/155243576422233818' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1344012943"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 5, 2007 at 11:55 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3586982541249398487</id><published>2007-05-05T01:31:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-05T01:31:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Will, on a positive note, bravo for the format cha...</title><content type='html'>Will, on a positive note, bravo for the format changes.  I was Mr. &quot;anonymous&quot; who hoped you&#39;d look at the changes as being for the better and I can see you took it seriously.  Congrats!  It&#39;ll only mean more comments, and more back and forth amongst us all, and thats ALL GOOD!&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;BTW... I&#39;ve recently joined the ranks of the &quot;unwashed&quot; unemployed this past month... hangin around the house and just bumming.  It feels really weird.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/3586982541249398487'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/3586982541249398487'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html?showComment=1178350260000#c3586982541249398487' title=''/><author><name>DrFix</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/13996714804361467430</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-155243576422233818' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/155243576422233818' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-388975791"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 5, 2007 at 1:31 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-2570916786155275638</id><published>2007-05-05T01:27:00.000-06:00</published><updated>2007-05-05T01:27:00.000-06:00</updated><title type='text'>Rush, the first cerebral rock band I hooked onto b...</title><content type='html'>Rush, the first cerebral rock band I hooked onto back in the late 70&#39;s.  It wasn&#39;t a &quot;chick&quot; band because you actually had to think!&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Still, back to topic, well just how many more taserings have to happen?  Lord!  Seems every other day they&#39;re zapping somebody for the slightest reasons and even gunning them  while in the throes of agony.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;If someone cause me to drop my child like that I might be up on assault charges for beating the clowns who tasered me to a pulp.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/2570916786155275638'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/155243576422233818/comments/default/2570916786155275638'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html?showComment=1178350020000#c2570916786155275638' title=''/><author><name>DrFix</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/13996714804361467430</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2007/05/default-setting-is-overkill.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-155243576422233818' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/155243576422233818' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-388975791"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="May 5, 2007 at 1:27 AM"/></entry></feed>